# 基本図形編集のプロセスで文字枠の中を仮身化する (design 11.3), for tools/ui_run.py: a figure
# of 30 small rectangles, two zigzag lines and one piece of text "ABC" (mkbig fig 30 4 1; its
# box from 100,120 to 220,160 of the figure, 210,247 to 330,287 on the screen). The same is
# done with the desktop's figure editor and with the one running as a process: the text
# pressed twice to edit it, "BC" picked (the caret after A, Shift+End), Ctrl+9, the name
# offered ("BC") taken with Enter, Escape to end the editing, the figure saved. The figure's
# record 0 comes out the same but for the UUIDs (the new object's and the link's own), and
# the new object's record 0 and its name come out the same, byte for byte.
# Keys: Home 4A, Right 4F, End 4D (Shift 02), 9 26 (Ctrl 01), Enter 28, Esc 29; Ctrl+S 16,
# Ctrl+E 08.
# the desktop's figure editor opened by open, whatever the program object says (figproc kernel)
figproc kernel
mkbig fig 30 4 1
open big
waitwin 画用紙 600
sync 600
wait 500
dclick 215 255
sync 600
key 4A
key 4F
key 4D 02
sync 600
key 26 01
wait 800
shot virt_kernel_name
key 28
wait 800
sync 600
shot virt_kernel_link
key 29
sync 600
key 16 01
sync 600
sum show anon
keep kernel_fig
sum show link
keep kernel_new
key 08 01
sync 600
wait 500
mkbig fig 30 4 1
logmark
pfig big
expectsincein 60 figure: opened 画用紙 shapes 33
wait 500
logmark
dclick 215 255
expectsince figure: text editing begun
key 4A
key 4F
key 4D 02
wait 300
logmark
key 26 01
expectsince figure: name panel open
wait 300
shot virt_process_name
logmark
key 28
expectsince figure: a new object kept (0)
wait 300
shot virt_process_link
logmark
key 29
expectsince figure: text editing ended
logmark
key 16 01
expectsince figure: saved (0)
sum show anon
same kernel_fig
sum show link
same kernel_new
key 08 01
expect figure: closed
